<p>Large crowds rallied in several cities over the weekend of February 14–15, calling for political change in Iran. The biggest gatherings were in Munich, timed alongside the Munich Security Conference. Police estimates cited by multiple outlets put the Munich crowd at roughly 200,000 to 250,000. Separate reports also described another large rally in the Toronto area, though crowd-size figures varied by outlet. The demonstrations showed how organized and far-reaching the diaspora campaign has become. Participants waved pre-revolution Iranian flags and urged foreign leaders meeting nearby to take a tougher line on Tehran. Reza Pahlavi, the exiled son of Iran’s last monarch, addressed supporters and said he was ready to help lead a transition toward a secular, democratic future; some coverage also said he pressed for stronger U.S. action.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/6xuScc8FGtz39XhiKUzUvOSiws1Z2Le2EWaatybzwJZXXtSIP15k4tL8ryCv1ttWQxWU_B2QdZ3nZlE0rm3K8B5Q56rd6j0U_oVnmE7H-VrWB8Jbd1Y_BREDECOsSGNT3SXrvgErix-5zqnWqLaVOJE584xpejWhSzQw14hB7WE0cjniC39Lx31XYIEZAdNKlQeLnc-ObZ8a-QVCtFU' alt='Protesters hold pre-revolution Iranian flags during a Munich demonstration held alongside the Munich Security Conference.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Pressure on Tehran: Organizers framed the rallies as a message to leaders gathering for the Munich Security Conference, urging tougher measures—especially sanctions—against Iran’s leadership.</li><li>Diplomacy continues: Al‑Monitor reported that Switzerland confirmed Oman would mediate a fresh round of talks in Geneva next week, and the New York Times said more U.S.-Iran talks were expected Tuesday.</li><li>Crackdown spotlight: Coverage linked the demonstrations to anger over a deadly crackdown inside Iran, as families shared footage online commemorating relatives who were shot during nationwide anti-government protests.</li><li>Who turned out in Munich: Al‑Monitor described a largely pro-monarchist crowd that traveled from across Europe, rallying under a “sea of flags,” while Reza Pahlavi told supporters he wants to help lead Iran toward a democratic future.</li><li>Global spread: Beyond Germany and Canada, reports described rallies in cities including Melbourne, Athens, Tokyo and London—another sign of the diaspora campaign’s reach.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Reza Pahlavi (exiled royal figure): Speaking to a mass rally in Munich, he said he was ready to help lead Iran toward a &quot;secular democratic future&quot; as demonstrators called for an end to the Islamic Republic’s leadership. (<a href='https://www.al-monitor.com/originals/2026/02/250000-rally-germany-demand-game-over-irans-leaders'>Al-Monitor</a>)</li><li>US President Donald Trump: Al‑Monitor quoted him as saying a change of power in Iran would be the &quot;best thing&quot;. (<a href='https://www.al-monitor.com/originals/2026/02/son-irans-last-shah-urges-us-action-supporters-rally-munich'>Al-Monitor</a>)</li><li>Iranian government and US officials (Al Jazeera account): Al Jazeera described Iran and the US trading sharp statements as diaspora rallies abroad called for action. (<a href='https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/2/14/iran-us-spar-as-diaspora-organises-rallies-abroad-calling-for-action'>Al Jazeera</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.reddit.com/r/worldnews/comments/1r4yjl5/north_york_demonstration_draws_350000_in_support/'>North York demonstration draws 350,000 in support of anti-government protesters in Iran: Toronto police</a> - reddit.com</li><li><a href='https://www.nytimes.com/2026/02/14/world/europe/iran-regime-rallies-munich.html'>Thousands Rally for Iran Regime Change in Cities Around the World</a> - nytimes.com</li><li><a href='http://www.euronews.com/video/2026/02/14/more-than-200000-in-munich-rally-for-reza-pahlavi-and-regime-change-in-iran'>More than 200,000 in Munich rally for Reza Pahlavi and regime change in Iran</a> - euronews.com</li><li><a href='https://www.aljazeer